"""Reading the persisted state of a simulator's embedded web application.

Applications built on the embedded browser keep their state in the local
storage of the origin they are served from.  WebKit persists that storage as
a SQLite database named ``localstorage.sqlite3`` inside the application's
WebKit website-data directory, with one row per stored key.  Values written
by the page are JSON text encoded as UTF-16, and recent writes may still live
in the database's write-ahead log rather than in the main file.

The readers here expose that state without altering it: the database and its
sidecars are opened through a private copy, so evaluation observes everything
the page committed while the simulator's own files stay untouched.
"""

